# No writer drift (RC-226 / RC-452)

The operator selects **ACTIVE_WRITER** per mission. Claude and Cursor may both implement. Neither has permanent writer or auditor status.

## Law

When `pm_mission.json` is in-progress (`active` / `ready_for_claude` / `ready_for_writer` / `in_progress`) and `active_writer` ≠ current agent, **do not Edit/Write/StrReplace mission `scope_paths`**. Process-surface allowlist only. This is concurrency protection (one canonical worktree, one active writer), not an identity ban.

## Mechanical enforcers (not this `.mdc`)

- `tools/writer_drift_lock.py` + `pm_mission_edit_violation` via `process_lock_guard.py` (PreToolUse — deny message starts `SOD_DRIFT:`)
- `check_writer_no_drift` / `check_active_writer_law` in `tools/check_institutional_correctness.py`
- Escape: `ED_WRITER_DRIFT_GUARD=off` / `ED_PM_MISSION_GUARD=off` (operator only, visible)

## Halt

`STOP` / `PAUSE` / `HANG IT UP` / `DO NOT CONTINUE`
